course: dictionary
lesson: 10693
title: Unrolling and reading context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word unroll means to open out something that was rolled up so it lies flat. A map, a poster or a sleeping bag can all unroll. «A hedgehog rolls into a tight prickly ball when frightened.» Rolled up tight is the opposite of unrolled, so you can see the two ideas work together.
explain: Use the words around a new word to check its meaning. «Badgers are strong enough to unroll one.» A hedgehog that is curled up tight is hard to open, so unroll must mean to pull it open and flat. Read the sentence again with your meaning in place of the word to see if it makes sense.
explain: Unroll can also mean to become open and flat after being rolled. In maths, you can unroll a tube (a cylinder) to see a rectangle. That rectangle helps you work out the surface area of the tube.
fact: Unroll means to open out something rolled up so it lies flat.
fact: «Unroll» can also mean to become open and flat after being rolled.
fact: A hedgehog has about 5,000 to 7,000 spines, which are hollow hairs without barbs.
fact: «Badgers are strong enough to unroll one» shows that a curled-up hedgehog can be opened out.
fact: Unrolling a cylinder (a tube) shows a rectangle, which helps you find its surface area.
exercise: Mia unrolls her sleeping bag at the campsite. What does unroll mean here? | Throw it in the bin | *Open out so it lies flat | Wrap up tightly | Fold it in half
exercise: Ben has a poster rolled up tight. He wants to unroll it. What does he do? | He ties it in a knot | He rolls it even tighter | *He opens it out flat on the table | He cuts it into pieces
exercise: A tube is cut and unrolled on paper. What shape do you see? | *A rectangle | A circle | A triangle | A cube
test: «A hedgehog rolls into a tight prickly ball when frightened, which is why Carroll made hedgehogs into croquet balls that unroll and walk away.» What does unroll mean in this sentence? | Shrink to nothing | Roll up tighter | *Open out so it lies flat | Hide under a leaf
test: Why does unrolling a tube help with maths? | It shows a circle, which helps you find its weight | *It shows a rectangle, which helps you find its surface area | It turns the tube into a cube | It makes the tube lighter
exam: Which word means the same as unroll? | Hide | *Open out | Roll up | Crush
